  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 953 PM CDT Sun Aug 23 2026\n\nOur next rain chances start to develop on Wednesday as a surface\nlow comes together over the Arklatex and develops a boundary\nacross the Gulf Coast states and into the Tennessee Valley. It's\nnot a lot to work with, but we do introduce low to medium PoPs\nWednesday and Wednesday night, with rain chances tapering off on\nThursday as the system pulls off to the east. Although there will\nbe some storm chances, QPF values are somewhat anemic, and we\ncertainly aren't outlooked for any severe storms for the\nforeseeable future. Temperatures will warm up to seasonal values \nby Wednesday, with readings staying close to seasonal norms \nthrough the weekend, then warming up a bit to start off next \nweek.",
